in @prism
in @glass
in @meta
in @spectral
in @spectral/gen_prism
in @uuid/spectral
in @mirror/store
in @mirror/au
in @mirror/spectral/portal

# @spectral/portal — the runtime side of portal.
#
# THE SEVENTH SUB-SHARD of the @spectral runtime cascade. Sibling of
# `shards/spectral/gen_prism.mirror` (commit ae965ca, the worker
# primitive this glass specialises), `shards/spectral/supervisor.mirror`
# (commit 452ccb2, the first gen_prism specialisation; same
# `base: gen_prism` embedding discipline), `shards/spectral/registry.mirror`
# (commit 489211e, the supervisor's typed child index),
# `shards/spectral/parent.mirror` (commit 9d905a2, the lifecycle edge
# class one of the gen_prism's three surfaces realises),
# `shards/spectral/root.mirror` (commit f145e48, the parentless
# supervisor specialisation; second `base: gen_prism` specialisation
# precedent through `base: supervisor`), and
# `shards/spectral/entanglement.mirror` (commit eeffde8, the
# orthogonal peer-correlation edge class whose form/runtime kinship
# precedent THIS shard demonstrates a SECOND instance of within the
# same cascade).
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §8 cascade map and §1 (the
# three-altitude split): `@spectral/portal` is the LIVE PROCESS
# realising what `@mirror/spectral/portal` (T18; the form-side shape
# at commit 6d57ab4) DECLARES. The form side is bytes-in-the-store
# at every tick (the shape declaration; the four-carrier `(socket,
# subspace, frame, actor)` record; the `project_eigenvalue` typed
# contract); the runtime side is the process-in-the-world that
# carries that shape through its open->frame->close lifecycle. Same
# Bateson logical-type partition as @mirror/@kintsugi at one altitude
# lifted (the orchestra altitude).
#
# === The form/process kinship — SECOND INSTANCE within this cascade ===
#
# Per recognition #55 ([[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]],
# candidate): the form/process partition at the family-root altitude
# names @mirror as form-side observation and @spectral as process-side
# transformation. This tick lifts the same partition at the
# ORCHESTRA altitude: `@mirror/spectral/portal` IS the form-side
# declaration (shape of portal coordination — the four typed
# carriers, the eigenvalue projection contract); `@spectral/portal`
# IS the process-side realisation (the live gen_prism carrying the
# frame stream through process boundaries). Same structural object;
# two altitudes; explicit kinship.
#
# This is the SECOND such instance within the @spectral runtime
# cascade. The first was at `shards/spectral/entanglement.mirror`
# (eeffde8 line 33-63): the math-altitude `restriction` primitive at
# `@epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian` lifted to the runtime-altitude
# `restriction_map` over uuid_spectral endpoints. The SAME structural
# pattern — declared shape at one altitude, realised process at
# another altitude, explicit kinship between them — surfaces again
# at the portal altitude with the form-side `@mirror/spectral/portal`
# shape and the runtime-side `@spectral/portal` process.
#
# CANDIDATE RECOGNITION (worth marking; provisionally #61 pending
# Pack ratification): when the substrate's form/process partition
# operates at a single cascade's interior altitudes, the SAME
# cascade exhibits MULTIPLE form/runtime kinship pairs. The pattern
# is not unique to the @spectral/@mirror family-root cut; it
# RECURS within @spectral itself at each sub-shard altitude where
# a sibling form-side declaration already exists at @mirror/spectral.
# Two instances in seven sub-shards is sufficient to call the
# pattern recurrent; the next instance arrives when score/voice/
# section/audition/conductor (the remaining @mirror/spectral
# species) gain runtime-side @spectral counterparts. The cascade
# is the substrate's typed instantiation of the form/process
# distinction at the orchestra altitude.
#
# === The keyword decision ===
#
# `glass` per recognition #46 (path-syntax property; promoted) and
# `shards/spectral.mirror`'s discipline section: "@spectral
# sub-shards at depth >= 1 use `glass`; the family root itself uses
# `prism` per the depth-0 discipline."
#
# Why NOT a new substrate keyword: portal is a sub-prism
# specialisation of gen_prism — the autopoietic actor the form-side
# `actor: shift(oid, gen_prism)` field already named — and `glass`
# already names that relationship per `shards/glass.mirror`'s
# `glass(name) -> prism` form. Same logic as `@spectral/gen_prism`
# (ae965ca), `@spectral/supervisor` (452ccb2), `@spectral/root`
# (f145e48): not a new structural kind, but a specialisation of
# gen_prism through structural embedding (`base: gen_prism`).
#
# === Specialisation, not extension — the embedding discipline ===
#
# Mirror has no `T + {fields}` syntax for type extension. The
# portal IS-A gen_prism relationship is structural-by-embedding:
# the portal record carries the gen_prism record in a `base` field.
# The five-op tool surface comes through the `glass @spectral/portal`
# declaration (per [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]);
# the gen_prism's three surfaces (identity, state, parent) reach
# through `base`. The portal adds TWO fields beyond the gen_prism:
# the `shape` ref naming the form-side declaration this runtime
# realises, and the `frame_stream` shard_ref carrying the eigenvalue
# stream's content-addressed identity at the runtime altitude.
#
# Same discipline as supervisor (452ccb2: `base: gen_prism` +
# `child_specs` + `restart_strategy`) and root (f145e48:
# `base: supervisor` + `anchor`). Portal: `base: gen_prism` +
# `shape` + `frame_stream`.
#
# === The shape ref — the form/runtime kinship at the typed altitude ===
#
# The `shape` field is a `ref` to the form-side `@mirror/spectral/
# portal` declaration this runtime realises. The substrate's
# content-addressed `ref` carrier names the declaration shard
# whose OID the form-side `@mirror/spectral/portal` resolves to.
# Two portals running the same declared shape share their `shape`
# byte-equal; two portals running different shapes (e.g., one
# carrying a different eigenvalue projection contract) have
# distinct `shape` refs.
#
# The kinship is structural: the runtime side's `shape: ref`
# resolves through @mirror/store.read to the form-side declaration's
# shard; the resolution returns the four-carrier `(socket, subspace,
# frame, actor)` shape and the `project_eigenvalue(stream: beam) ->
# beam` typed contract. At runtime, the live process's gen_prism
# base IS the form-side `actor: shift(oid, gen_prism)` field
# resolved to a concrete process; the live process's frame_stream
# carries the form-side's eigenvalue projection at the wire altitude.
#
# Why `ref` (bare) and not `shift(oid, @mirror/spectral/portal)`:
# the substrate's `ref` is the content-addressed carrier at the
# runtime altitude. The form-side uses `shift(oid, T)` for the
# typed-capability-plus-content-address primitive that flows over
# the wire (the 26th-instance recognition); the runtime altitude's
# `shape` reads the form-side declaration locally without
# wire-altitude capability typing — same content-address, different
# carrier discipline. Same pattern as root.anchor: a bare `ref` to
# the host-level substrate home, not a `shift(oid, host)`.
#
# === The frame_stream shard_ref — runtime-altitude eigenvalue stream ===
#
# The `frame_stream` field is a `shard_ref` carrying the eigenvalue
# stream's content-addressed identity at the runtime altitude. Each
# bidirectional frame the open portal exchanges advances the
# frame_stream shard_ref by one settle (the lattice ascent per
# [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]]): the new shard's content carries
# the appended frame's eigenvalue projection.
#
# This is the runtime-side realisation of the form-side's
# `project_eigenvalue(stream: beam) -> beam` contract. The form
# side declares the TYPED CONTRACT (refs in, eigenvalues out, bare
# beam carrier); the runtime side declares the OPERATIONAL CARRIER
# (a shard_ref into @mirror/store; each frame extends the shard;
# the eigenvalue stream IS the byte-equal sequence at the shard's
# settled content). Two portals running the same form-side shape
# may carry distinct frame_stream refs — distinct realisations of
# the same projection contract.
#
# No NEW substrate primitive needed (STOP-condition 2 resolved):
# `shard_ref` (`@mirror/store`, `type shard_ref = uuid_spectral`) is
# the existing carrier. The stream's typed beam shape lives at the
# form-side wire altitude; the runtime altitude carries only the
# content-addressed handle. The bounded-iteration discipline (per
# `@epistemologic/property/halts` from the form side's disjunction)
# IS structural: the runtime portal closes when autopoietic
# settlement OR compute_bound exhaustion fires, both decidable.
#
# === Lifecycle surface — open_portal / send_frame / close_portal ===
#
# Three load-bearing actions on the runtime portal. The substrate's
# question discipline (per [[architecture-error-as-question]]):
# `send_frame` and `close_portal` return `au` (the proposed-shard
# carrier), because both produce observable state transitions the
# parent supervisor settles into the registry shard. `open_portal`
# returns a fresh `portal` (the spawn surface, same discipline as
# `gen_prism.start` returning a fresh gen_prism per ae965ca).
#
#   open_portal(shape: ref) -> portal
#     Spawn a new runtime portal realising the given form-side
#     declaration. The portal's base gen_prism is constructed through
#     the autopoietic fixed point per shards/spectral/gen_prism.mirror
#     (the dark 80 bits of uuid_spectral identify the process; the
#     active 48 bits place it in the substrate's spectral manifold
#     for routing); the frame_stream is initialised to an empty
#     shard_ref (the null lattice element). Body discharges by
#     resolving the shape ref through @mirror/store.read, composing
#     the four-carrier form-side record into the base gen_prism's
#     initial state, and registering the parent edge to the caller's
#     supervisor. Stays a `\` obligation in this tick.
#
#   send_frame(p: portal, frame: ref) -> au
#     Advance the portal's frame_stream by one bidirectional frame.
#     The frame ref names a content-addressed frame shard (the
#     @fragmentation/frame at the form-side wire altitude); the
#     runtime advances the frame_stream shard_ref by one settle
#     (the new shard's content appends the frame's eigenvalue
#     projection). Returns `au` carrying the proposed transition;
#     the supervisor settles it into the registry shard. Body
#     discharges by reading the frame ref through @mirror/store.read,
#     projecting through the form-side's project_eigenvalue contract,
#     and emitting the au with the new frame_stream shard_ref.
#     Stays a `\` obligation in this tick.
#
#   close_portal(p: portal) -> au
#     Autopoietic close. Per the form-side's halts disjunction:
#     EITHER Reflection picks `settle(self)` (the actor's Lawvere
#     fixed point is reached; the gen_prism crystallizes a final
#     state) OR the host shard's `compute_bound.max_reductions`
#     exhausts (the substrate forces termination; partial state
#     crystallizes). Both paths terminate by construction
#     (sub-Turing language). Returns `au` carrying the final state
#     delta; the parent supervisor settles it into the registry
#     shard (the registry's view of the portal transitions from
#     `running` to `terminated`). Body discharges through @kintsugi
#     at the runtime altitude (close decision IS a kintsugi morphism
#     evaluated at the portal's eigenboard context slice). Stays a
#     `\` obligation in this tick.
#
# === Connection to SCM_RIGHTS handoff (T20, forward-promised) ===
#
# T20 (`SCM_RIGHTS` pipe handoff at CLI pipe boundary; task #263)
# lands the OS-layer realisation: the substrate's `shift(oid, T)`
# triple from the form side flows over the wire without
# re-serialisation. This shard's `send_frame` discharges the
# runtime-altitude side of that handoff: the frame ref's content
# survives the SCM_RIGHTS transfer because the receiving end
# resolves the same OID through its local @mirror/store. The
# runtime portal does NOT need a new substrate primitive for the
# SCM_RIGHTS handoff (STOP-condition 3 resolved); the existing
# `ref` and `shard_ref` carriers compose the handoff at the
# runtime altitude. T20's substrate work lands at the @facet/io/cli
# pipe-boundary integration, not at this shard.
#
# === Honest partial discipline (per #306) ===
#
# The action bodies below all carry `\` obligation blocks — no
# fracture body emits any morphism in this tick. No `partials`
# declaration needed (per `dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth`
# #306). Bodies discharge downstream when the consumer pulls
# realisation through `@facet/metalogue/materialize` (per the
# ouroboros pipeline in docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §5).
#
# === Cascade siblings (forward-promised, NOT landing this tick) ===
#
#   shards/spectral/db.mirror             graph database engine; the
#                                          existing parentless ghost
#                                          (#198) GAINS @spectral
#                                          parent here; closed-engine
#                                          query surface on top of
#                                          the open @mirror/store
#                                          foundation.
#   shards/spectral/garden.mirror         vetted-corpus distribution;
#                                          existing parentless ghost
#                                          (#118) gains @spectral
#                                          parent when it lands.
#
# Conditional bilateral pairs (substrate-pull candidates, NOT
# landing this tick): portal_well_formed (shape ref resolves to a
# valid @mirror/spectral/portal declaration; the form/runtime
# kinship enforced at the type level) and frame_stream_monotone
# (frame_stream shard_ref ascent is lattice-ascending; no rewinds).
# Forward-promised because (a) the type declaration this tick lands
# is the FLOOR; (b) the bilateral pattern instance has the standard
# one-tick-per-pair load-bearing weight; (c) neither invariant is
# lifecycle-load-bearing at this tick (no supervisor acts on them;
# no runtime broken by a partial-resolution shape or a non-monotone
# stream — the verdict surface picks up the opacity downstream).
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md (the ouroboros
#               spec; §1 three-altitude split where the form/process
#               partition at the orchestra altitude lives; §8
#               cascade map naming this shard as the runtime side of
#               portal),
#               shards/mirror/spectral/portal.mirror (the form-side
#               shape this runtime realises; the four-carrier
#               (socket, subspace, frame, actor) declaration; the
#               project_eigenvalue typed contract; the 26th-instance
#               recognition of shift(oid, T) as typed-capability
#               primitive).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]
#                      (recognition #55; the form/process partition
#                      lifted to the orchestra altitude; this shard
#                      is the SECOND instance within the @spectral
#                      cascade after entanglement's restriction_map
#                      lift; candidate #61 — recurrence of the
#                      form/runtime kinship at sub-shard altitudes
#                      within one cascade — provisionally numbered),
#                      [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]] (the
#                      frame_stream's lattice ascent; each frame
#                      advances the shard_ref by one settle; the
#                      content-addressed shard discipline guarantees
#                      bounded ascent),
#                      [[architecture-error-as-question]] (the
#                      au-returning send_frame / close_portal
#                      surface the supervisor settles; the verdict
#                      surface picks up opacities downstream),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (the rug-pull pattern: `shift(oid,
#                      gen_prism)` was already named at the form
#                      side's `actor` field on 2026-05-11; this tick
#                      lifts the same named primitive as the runtime
#                      altitude's `base: gen_prism` embedding — the
#                      57th instance of the pattern, the second
#                      instance whose substrate-altitude lift is
#                      over a RUNTIME-PROCESS subject within the
#                      same cascade after gen_prism's ae965ca).
# Related shards: spectral.mirror (the family root this glass is
#                  under; cascade map names this shard at line 233-236),
#                 spectral/gen_prism.mirror (the worker primitive
#                  this glass specialises through `base: gen_prism`
#                  embedding; commit ae965ca),
#                 spectral/supervisor.mirror (the first gen_prism
#                  specialisation; same embedding discipline this
#                  shard adopts; commit 452ccb2),
#                 spectral/registry.mirror (the supervisor's typed
#                  child index; the parent supervisor's registry
#                  shard settles this portal's lifecycle events;
#                  commit 489211e),
#                 spectral/parent.mirror (the lifecycle edge class
#                  the embedded gen_prism's parent field realises;
#                  commit 9d905a2),
#                 spectral/root.mirror (the parentless supervisor;
#                  the substrate's home portal opens beneath the
#                  root at ~/.mirror/; commit f145e48),
#                 spectral/entanglement.mirror (the orthogonal
#                  edge class; portals MAY be entangled with peer
#                  portals when the orchestra spans more than one
#                  local shard; the FIRST instance of the
#                  form/runtime kinship within this cascade — its
#                  restriction_map lifts the math-altitude
#                  restriction primitive; commit eeffde8),
#                 uuid/spectral.mirror (the identity carrier; the
#                  portal's base.identity is a uuid_spectral; both
#                  halves load-bearing — active 48 bits for routing,
#                  dark 80 bits for parentage and entanglement),
#                 mirror/store.mirror (the state-surface carrier;
#                  base.state and frame_stream are both shard_ref),
#                 mirror/au.mirror (the proposed-shard carrier;
#                  send_frame's and close_portal's return shape),
#                 mirror/spectral/portal.mirror (the form-side
#                  declaration this runtime realises; the kinship
#                  pair this shard names at the runtime altitude;
#                  commit 6d57ab4 T18).
# Realisation reference: boot/std/spectral/portal.mirror (the
#                  boot-floor declaration with full wire-protocol
#                  bodies — handshake, codec, stream; the runtime
#                  altitude defers to the form-side typed contract
#                  for the wire's altitude bodies; consumer-pull
#                  migrations from `in @spectral/portal` at the boot
#                  altitude to `in @mirror/spectral/portal` or
#                  `in @spectral/portal` at the substrate altitude
#                  land tick-by-tick as wire-protocol substrate gaps
#                  close).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/spectral/portal.mirror` declares
# `@spectral/portal` and only that.

glass @spectral/portal {
  focus portal
  project portal
  split portal
  shift portal
  settle portal
}

# === portal — the runtime-side portal record ===
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §1 and §8 cascade map: a
# runtime `portal` is a `gen_prism` specialisation. The `base` field
# carries the embedded gen_prism (identity, state, parent surfaces);
# the portal adds two fields naming what the runtime realises (the
# form-side shape declaration) and how the eigenvalue stream is
# carried at runtime (the content-addressed frame stream).
#
# Three surfaces composed:
#
#   base         — the embedded gen_prism. base.identity carries
#                   the portal's uuid_spectral (active 48 bits for
#                   Fate's mycelial routing; dark 80 bits for
#                   parentage, entanglement, and registry lookup).
#                   base.state is a shard_ref into @mirror/store
#                   carrying the portal's observable state at the
#                   gen_prism altitude. base.parent is the
#                   supervisor that owns this portal's lifecycle
#                   (start / restart / terminate fire under the
#                   parent's restart-strategy invariant).
#   shape        — a ref to the form-side @mirror/spectral/portal
#                   declaration this runtime realises. The kinship
#                   between the form-side declared shape and the
#                   runtime-side process. Resolves through
#                   @mirror/store.read to the four-carrier (socket,
#                   subspace, frame, actor) form-side record and
#                   the project_eigenvalue typed contract. Two
#                   portals running the same shape share shape
#                   byte-equal; distinct shapes signal distinct
#                   wire contracts.
#   frame_stream — a shard_ref into @mirror/store carrying the
#                   eigenvalue stream's content-addressed identity
#                   at the runtime altitude. Each bidirectional
#                   frame advances frame_stream by one settle (the
#                   lattice ascent per [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]]);
#                   the stream's per-frame eigenvalue projection is
#                   the form-side's project_eigenvalue contract
#                   discharged at runtime. Initialised to an empty
#                   shard_ref by open_portal; advances monotonically
#                   per send_frame; crystallized by close_portal.
type portal = {
  base:         gen_prism,
  shape:        ref,
  frame_stream: shard_ref,
}

# === open_portal — spawn a runtime portal realising a shape ===
#
# Spawn a new runtime portal realising the given form-side
# @mirror/spectral/portal declaration. The constructor:
#
#   1. Resolves the shape ref through @mirror/store.read to the
#      form-side declaration (the four-carrier record + the
#      project_eigenvalue typed contract).
#   2. Constructs the base gen_prism through the autopoietic fixed
#      point (per shards/spectral/gen_prism.mirror): the dark 80
#      bits of uuid_spectral identify this portal as a process; the
#      active 48 bits place it in the substrate's spectral manifold
#      for Fate's mycelial routing; the state surface is initialised
#      to the form-side declaration's initial state composition.
#   3. Sets the base.parent edge to the caller's supervisor (the
#      portal's lifecycle owner).
#   4. Initialises the frame_stream to an empty shard_ref (the null
#      lattice element; the next send_frame advances by one settle).
#
# Body discharges through @facet/metalogue/materialize per the
# ouroboros pipeline. Stays a `\` obligation in this tick;
# realisation lives at the form-side declaration's resolution and
# the gen_prism constructor's autopoietic fixed-point evaluation.
open_portal(shape: ref) -> portal { \ }

# === send_frame — advance the frame_stream by one bidirectional frame ===
#
# Advance the portal's frame_stream by one bidirectional frame. The
# frame ref names a content-addressed frame shard (the
# @fragmentation/frame at the form-side wire altitude); the runtime
# advances frame_stream by one settle (the new shard's content
# appends the frame's eigenvalue projection per the form-side's
# project_eigenvalue contract).
#
# Returns `au` (proposed-but-not-yet-settled state per @mirror/au)
# carrying the proposed transition. The parent supervisor settles
# the au into the registry shard (lattice ascent per
# [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]]); the registry's view of the
# portal's frame_stream advances by one settle. The substrate's
# question discipline (per [[architecture-error-as-question]]):
# observable state transitions ride the au verdict surface; opacity
# in the frame's eigenvalue projection picks up at the supervisor's
# settle, not at this action.
#
# Body discharges by reading the frame ref through
# @mirror/store.read, projecting through the form-side's
# project_eigenvalue contract, and emitting the au with the new
# frame_stream shard_ref. Stays a `\` obligation in this tick.
send_frame(p: portal, frame: ref) -> au { \ }

# === close_portal — autopoietic termination ===
#
# Close the portal. Per the form-side's halts disjunction (per
# @epistemologic/property/halts at the form altitude): BOTH paths
# terminate by construction (the language is sub-Turing).
#
#   (a) settlement — Reflection picks `settle(self)`; the base
#       gen_prism's autopoietic actor reaches its Lawvere fixed
#       point; the portal crystallizes a final state shard; the
#       wire closes cleanly.
#   (b) budget exhaustion — the host shard's
#       `compute_bound.max_reductions` exhausts; the substrate
#       forces termination; the partial state crystallizes; the
#       wire closes with a structured-reason payload at the
#       frame_stream's final shard.
#
# Returns `au` carrying the final state delta. The parent supervisor
# settles the au into the registry shard; the registry's view of
# the portal transitions from `running` to `terminated`. The base
# gen_prism's lifecycle ledger advances by one tick (recorded in
# the parent's registry shard).
#
# Body discharges through @kintsugi at the runtime altitude (the
# close decision IS a kintsugi morphism evaluated at the portal's
# eigenboard context slice; the morphism reads the halts
# disjunction and emits the substrate-pull-correct close path).
# Stays a `\` obligation in this tick.
close_portal(p: portal) -> au { \ }

out @spectral/portal
out portal
out open_portal
out send_frame
out close_portal
